2 CONT Meginhard V. von Formbach, Count of Windberg, was born circa 1027 to Thiemo II von Formbach (?-1040) and Tochter von Braunschweig (?-?) and died 21 February 1066 of battle wounds. He married Mathilde von Rheinhausen . Notable ance
2 CONC stors include Charlemagne (747-814), Alfred the Great (849-899). Ancestors are from France, Belgium, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT MEGINHARD [IV], son of [THIEMO [I] Graf von Schweinachgau, in Reichenhall und im Salzburggau [Formbach] & his wife ---] (-killed in battle 1066).  According to the 14th century Genealogia comitum Neuburgensium sive Formbacensium, 
2 CONC "Meginhardus frater senioris Tiemonis genuit Oudalricum, Hermannum provincie comitem et Chunradum"[2260], although it appears chronologically more probable that Meginhard was the son rather than brother of "senioris Tiemonis" cons
2 CONC idering that it is unlikely that Meginhard's sons were born much before [1045/50].  Wegener refers to abbot Wirnto's description of the foundation of the abbey of Vornbach dated [1108/27] which names "Meginhardus comes, Ekibertus 
2 CONC comes, Oudalricus comes supranominati [Meginhardi] filius et frater eius Hermannus comes et nepos Chounradi comes filius supradicti Oudalrici, Ekibertus comes, Heinricus comes et filius eius Dietricus comes"[2261].  Graf.  Vogt vo
2 CONC n Niederaltaich [1060].  "Heinricus…rex" donated property "villam Geroltisdorf in pago Bunnaha in comitatu Meginhardi comitis" to Kloster Gurk by charter dated 1066[2262]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [MECHTILD von Reinhausen, daughter of ELLE Graf [von Reinhausen] & his wife ---] (-1073 or after).  Reinhard Abbot of Reinhausen’s work about the family of Reinhard Bishop of Halberstadt names “Mathild et Rikence” as the two dau
2 CONC ghters of “Elle”, adding that Mechtild married “Bavro principi” by whom she had “Hermannum de Winzenburch”[2263].  The accuracy of this source is unknown, particularly because the name of Mechtild’s husband is recorded only in gen
2 CONC eral terms
