2 CONT Sophia van Rheineck, born circa 1115, daughter of Otto van Rheineck
2 CONT (van Salm) and Gertrud van Northeim. First mentioned at the consecration of the new abbey church of Egmond in October 1143.
2 CONT She was a very religious woman and made numerous donations to church institutions. She made a pilgrimage to Santiago de Compostola and repeatedly
2 CONT to Jerusalem (presumably with her husband in 1139, certainly as a widow in 1173 and 1176).
2 CONT Died on September 26, 1176, in Jerusalem (in the German Hospital). Buried in Jerusalem.
2 CONT Source: GN 1990, 375, 652; Lindemans, 100, 182; Van Wimersma, Quarters, 530.
2 CONT From this marriage:
2 CONT 1. Floris III van Holland (see 98.179.716).
2 CONT Source: Source: The ancestors of Niesje Elizabeth Smit (born 1922) by A. Bothof (published Oegstgeest, March 2007) @ https://www.onsvoorrijzen.nl/wp-content/plugins/typify-databank/dow...
