1 NAME Otto Bondosen /Snafs til Emmerlev Kjærgaard/ til Kjærgaard
2 GIVN Otto Bondosen
2 SURN Snafs til Emmerlev Kjærgaard
2 NSFX til Kjærgaard
2 _MARNM Snafs
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1358
2 PLAC Sønderjylland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1402
1 OCCU Godsejer & ridder
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.hammerweb.dk/1353.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT http://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/Snafs/Snafs.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Snafs
2 CONT
2 CONT This family originated in South Jutland, begins with a man called Bonde Snafs til Emmerlev Kjærgaard, known 1315. He had issue a son Otto Snafs, known 1361, died 1402, married Abel Albertsdatter (Eberstein; died after 1438). Their
2 CONC  issue follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Claus Snafs, known 1409-1411. 2. Hr. Otto Snafs, known 1411-1442, married Henrike van Hemskere (died after 1433). 3. Albert Snafs, known 1420-1438.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same arms were carried by a later family, perhaps descended from number 1, above, though no proof thereof exists. This line begins with a Henrik Clausen, known 1478-1494. He had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Claus Hansen, priest, known 1494. 2. Hans Hansen, provost, known 1512-1531. 3. Knud Hansen. 3.1. Anne, married Hans Vestfalling. 3.2. Kirsten, married 1stly the mayor of Assen Berild Pedersen (Pøiske?); married 2ndly the alderm
2 CONC an of Assen Hans Nielsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~corpusnobiliorum/snafs.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT kilde: http://lindevang-lolland.dk/index-filer/Page366.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Bondosen Snafs
2 CONT
2 CONT Død 1402
2 CONT
2 CONT Emmelev Kjærgård
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Snafs udstedte i 1361 i Tønder Vidne et pantebrev fra Hertug Valdemar til bispen i Ribe og udlagde da en gård i Emmelev, som han havde arvet efter sin fader  Bundodis Snafs
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT gert thiele.
