1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yet - this page claims that Johannes de Gristow also was Barnutas son and thus the brother of Dobislaw and not his son:
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote:
2 CONT
2 CONT "With his wife Slavomira, a daughter of Mitzlaw II von Gützkow according to the chronicler Kantzow , he founded the family of the Lords von Gristow . This only died out in modern times. His wife and sons Dobizlaus de Gristow (ment
2 CONC ioned 1237, 1249) and Johannes de Gristow (mentioned 1237, 1265, 1283, 1289) testified to his will shortly before his death, which Robert Klempin dated to the beginning of 1241. In it he gave the island of Koos to Eldena Monastery
2 CONC . His brother Wizlaw I confirmed the donation a few days after his death".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://second.wiki/wiki/barnuta
