1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HEINRICH [I] "der Kahle" von Stade, son of LOTHAR [II] Graf on Stade & his wife Swanehild --- (-11 May 976, bur Kloster Heeringen).  The paternity of Heinrich is determined from Thietmar recording the death of two 
2 CONC of his great grandfathers "both named Liuthar" at the battle of Lenzen 5 Sep[1808].  The Annalista Saxo refers to "Heinricus Calvus comes de Stathen" as "consanguineus" of Emperor Otto I[1809], but the precise relationship between
2 CONC  the two has not been identified.  Graf von Stade.  Graf im Heilangau 959: "Otto…rex" granted property "in pago…Helinge et Moside in locis…Buochstadon et Rinchurst in comitatu et legatione Heinrici comitis" to Magdeburg St Moritz 
2 CONC by charter dated 2 Jul 959[1810].  He constructed the castle of Harsefeld [Herseveld][1811] in 964.  Thietmar names his "grandfather Heinrich" when recording that he tried to capture Duke Hermann Billung at Magdeburg allegedly in 
2 CONC response the duke's "arrogance" in certain ceremonial matters[1812].  The Chronicon Monasterii Rosenfeld seu Hassefeld records the death “VI Id Mai” of “Heinricus comes, Calvus”[1813]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([946]) JUDITH, daughter of --- [Konradiner] & his wife --- (-16 Oct [973]).  "Iuditham sororem Udonis ducis qui postmodum in Calabria sub Ottone Rufo cum multis occubuit" is named in Annalista Saxo, which specifies that
2 CONC  she had three sons "Heinricum, Udonem et Sigefridum" and three daughters (unnamed), constructed the castle "qui Herseveld dicitur" and was buried with her husband (unnamed) at Heslinge[1814].  Her husband is named "Heinricus Calv
2 CONC us comes de Stathen" in a later passage[1815].  Thietmar records that his grandmother Judith died 26 Oct and "rests in a church which her daughter had constructed"[1816].  The necrology of Lüneburg records the death "16 Oct" of "J
2 CONC uthita com"[1817]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly HILDEGARD [von Reinhausen, daughter of ELLI [I] Graf von Reinhausen & his wife --] (-11 Jun --).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Heinrich [I] & his first wife had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''KUNIGUNDE von Stade ([956]-13 Jul 997, bur Germersleben).  The Annalista Saxo records the death in "Germersleve" on "III Id Iul 998" of "Cunigund comitissa uxor Sigefridi de Waldbike", specifies that she was sister o
2 CONC f "Heinrici, Sigefridi et Udonis" and names her five sons (in order) "Thietmarum, Sigefridum, Brunonem, Heinricum, Fridericum"[1843].  m (end 972) SIEGFRIED [I] "der Ältere" Graf von Walbeck, son of LOTHAR I Graf von Walbeck [Nord
2 CONC mark] & his wife Mathilde von Arneburg (-15/16 Mar 991).''' 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#KunigundeStadedied997
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Siegfried [I] & his wife had five children:''' 
2 CONT >i)          HEINRICH von Walbeck (973-killed in battle 1002 or after Sep 1004). 
2 CONT >ii)         FRIEDRICH von Walbeck (974-after 1012). 
2 CONT >iii)        THIETMAR von Walbeck (25 Jul 975-1 Dec1018).  
2 CONT >iv)       SIEGFRIED von Walbeck (-27 Nov 1032[1795]).  
2 CONT >v)        BRUNO von Walbeck (-21 Aug 1049).  
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#SiegfriedIWalbeckdied991
2 CONT ----
