2 CONC rkney Islands, Western Isles and Shetland Islands being given to Scotland in the formof a dowry.He could not count on the loyalty of his brothers who he had thrown into prison. One managed toescape and fled to England where Edward
2 CONC  IV recognised him as King of Scotland. This led to theconfederate lords attempting rebellion against James in 1488. James was defeated at the Battle ofSauchieburn. He was murdered after the battle by an assassin dressed in the ga
2 CONC rb of a priest.His marriage to Margaret was blessed with the births of James, James and John.
