1 NAME Johann /von Altenbockum/ II
2 GIVN Johann
2 NSFX II
2 _MARNM von Altenbockum
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1450
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1517
2 PLAC Karkeln
2 ADDR
1 OCCU seit 1493  Ritter, erw. 1492 , urk. 1500, 1517 tot  	auf Karkeln und Rothseden (belehnt 1501), Zehren (belehnt 1503),  	Klahnen (belehnt 1508) und Dursuppen, Kurland 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Making sense of the Altenbockum conundrum on Geni web site vs LDS pages
2 CONT Posting to Geni with links, to prove their family mash up is wrong.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geni page https://www.geni.com/people/Johann-von-Altenbockum-II/6000000021616889079?through=6000000010694818620 
2 CONT Lists :
2 CONT Johann von Altenbockum, II  
2 CONT Gender:	Male
2 CONT Birth:	circa 1450
2 CONT Death:	1517 (62-72)
2 CONT Karkeln
2 CONT Immediate Family:	Son of Johann I von Altenbockum and Thecla von Franck
2 CONT Husband of Elisabeth von Dönhoff and Catharina von Hahn
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Johann III von Altenbockum a.d.H. Dursuppen; 
2 CONT Philipp I von Altenbockum, a. Kallitzen; 
2 CONT Anna von Altenbockum; 
2 CONT Jasper von Altenbockum and 
2 CONT Georg von Altenbockum
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The problem with this arrangement, with no sources listed, is some assumptions have been made, and incorrectly joined Johann II to the wrong wife (Elisabeth von Dönhoff is not correct). This joining has also listed children under 
2 CONC the wrong couple arrangement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see the Latter Day Saints Geschlechtsregister 942-1942, which is scans (not indexed), of a huge collection of family tree chronologies. Hand written, with a great number of sources listed on the bottom of each page.
2 CONT My only struggle with these, is I do not read old German handwriting, so I am missing out on some context of each entry.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the accuracy of the family tree pages, I trust. These are also generally found in the Genealogy handbooks that have been printed for generations, and are in libraries around the world, and in some private collections. The
2 CONC se books have generally been treated as gospel, and a solid source, when researching our collective trees.
2 CONT
2 CONT OK, LDS page link to the von Altenbockum family tree, starts on page 16 of 391 images.
2 CONT Link to it is here: https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSPJ-5YS2?cat=325082&i=15
2 CONT On this page, listed as Tab 1, there is a Johann Ritter/Ritten (I am not quite sure of the spelling of this word/name), von Altenbockum. He is listed as the son of Johann von Altenbockum and Thekla von Frank.
2 CONT Johann Ritter is listed as married to Catharina von Hahn. 
2 CONT There is a reference behind her as on the ‘unknown page 2 of the von Hahn family group tree pages.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann and Catharina have 5 children listed here.
2 CONT Johann who x Elisabeth von Hahn (these are my direct ancestors)*****
2 CONT Philipp who x Dorothea (in pencil, hard to read) von Fircks(in ink, clear)
2 CONT Anna who x Jürgen von Hahn (these are my direct ancestors)*****
2 CONT Jasper who didn't marry (shows some notes with date ranges 1517 and 1561, but I can't understand the handwriting)
2 CONT and Georg who x unknown (shown as ....)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no mention on this page, that Johann, husband of Catharina, also married anyone else.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moving on to Elisabeth Dönhoff, shown on the Geni page, as wife of Johann II Altenbockum
2 CONT
2 CONT On the LDS pages, for the Dönhoff family, found here https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSGY-1S9L-9?cat=325082&i=200
2 CONT Image 201 of 435. This is shown as Tab 2 of the Dönhoff family pages
2 CONT The primary couple here is shown as Gerhard (stroked out and Hermann written in pencil) von Dönhoff, who married Maria Elisabeth von Dumpian.
2 CONT This couple has 7 children:
2 CONT Juditta who x Adoph von Lellis?
2 CONT Gerhard who x Elisabeth v d Osten-Sacken (her parents names are difficult to determine, there is stroke throughs and new pencil names I can’t decipher yet)
2 CONT filia (unnamed daughter) who x unknown v Franck/Fromck?
2 CONT Anna who x Johann v d Osten-Sacken
2 CONT Margarethe (Magdalena) who x Marcus von Fircks
2 CONT Dorothea who x Georg von Tolck?
2 CONT Elisabeth who x Johann von Altenbockum (with reference to the Unknown Altenbockum page, NOT to Tab 1 on the Altenbockum tree pages)
2 CONT
2 CONT Also of note, on the unknown page of the Altenbockum family (found here https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSPJ-5YXN?cat=325082&i=26 ), and on Tab 2 of the Dönhoff family (found here https://www.familysearch.org/ark:
2 CONC /61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSGY-1S9L-9?cat=325082&i=200 ), there are no dates listed, which does make this confusing to follow, especially when names were re-used so often in families.
2 CONT
2 CONT Therefore, I would like to request that the managers, using the source material from the LDS pages, realign the family group Johann II von Altenbockum to reflect the following:
2 CONT 1-Johann II married ONLY Catharina von Hahn (no parent info is known on her, she is on the unknown pages in the von Hahn group
2 CONT 2-Johann II and Catharina are full biological parents to all 5 children listed under Johann II
2 CONT 3-Elisabeth Dönhoff connection be removed from Johann II von Altenbockem, and aligned with the proper Johann Altenbockum, who has no parent or date info. 
2 CONT 4-Elisabeth’s parentage is correct and needs no edits.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you for your help.
2 CONT Jennifer Ferris
