1 OCCU Wojewode von Pommern,Schloß—Hauptrnann der Marienburga,  polnischer Kastelln von Danzig, Woiwode von Wenden und Pomerellen,Kgl. poln. Schiffs- u.Kriegskommissar für die Seefahrt 
1 TITL COUNT
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gerard Denhof (January 15, 1590 – December 23, 1648) – statesman and military figure of Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, commander of the German infantry (1621), castellan of Gdańsk (1642), voivode of Pomerania (164
2 CONC 3–1648), treasurer of the Prussian land (1643), marshal of the royal estate (1645), elder of Malbork, Koszeżyna, Viljandi, Lucinda and the economist of Malbork.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Descended from the German-Lithuanian Denhof family, owner of the coat of arms "Vepr". Son of the voivode of Dorpat Gerard Denhof (d. 1598?) and Margareta von Zweiffeln (d. 1622). Brothers – Ernest Magnus, Voivode of Pärnu (1581–16
2 CONC 42), Colonel German (d. 1620), Kasper, Voivode of Dorpat and Sieradz (1588–1645).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family and children===
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married twice. In 1629, his first marriage was to Katerina Opalinska (1596–1625), widow of Peter Opalinski, Crown scribe (1566–1600), and Elizabeth Zborovska, widow of Dmitriy Weicher, Castellan of Gdańsk (1578–1628), from 
2 CONC whom he had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In August 1637, he married for the second time Sibylle Margarita Brzeska (1620–1657), daughter of Jan Christian, Duke of Brzeska, Legnica and Scinowa (1591–1639) and Dorothea Sibylle of Brandenburg (1590–1625). Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Władysław (1639–1683), colonel of the infantry regiment (1664), commander of the royal guard, sub-cabinet of Pomerania (1668), castellan of Chełm (1677), voivode of Pomerania (1677–1683), treasurer of the Prussian land (1679), t
2 CONC he elder of Skarżewsk
2 CONT * Katerina Jadwiga (d. before 1668), 1st husband Voivode of Malbork Louis Weicher (d. 1656), 2nd husband from 1661 Voivode of Poznań Vaitiekus Konstantin Breza (c. 1620–1699)
2 CONT * Constance Anna, 1st husband Voivode of Chełm Jan Kos (d. 1662), 2nd husband Voivode of Malbork Jan Ignat Bakowski (c. 1615–1679)
2 CONT * Sibila, husband – Petras Ichlickis, a resident of Kalisz.
2 CONT
