2 CONT
2 CONT HERMANN [Billung] ([905/10]-Quedlinburg 27 Mar 973, bur Lüneburg St Michael).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Bilingus…filium Hermannum"[200].  His birth date range is estimated on the assumption that he was adult when appointed military commander in 936.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was given military command in Saxony ("princeps militiæ") by Otto I King of Germany in 936, which triggered the revolt of his brother Wichmann[201].
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf in Wetigau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Procurator of the king in Saxony 953, 961 and 966.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Otto…rex" granted property "Ozmina marcam…et Tarata marcam cum castello Grodista" to "vassallo Billing" by charter dated 26 Jun 952[202].  "Otto…rex" granted property to the church of St Moritz, Magdeburg by charter dated 953, wh
2 CONC ich names "Billingus…noster miles"[203].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf in dem Gauen Tilithi und Marstem 955.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Markgraf 956: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Otto…rex" granted rights to salt duties to Lüneburg St Mikhael at the request of "Herimanni marchionis" by charter dated 13 Aug 956[204].  "Otto…rex" gave property "in pago Usiti in comitatu comitis Willihelmi" to "nostro fideli 
2 CONC vasallo comitique Billinc" by charter dated 2 Dec 958[205], which may refer to Hermann Billung although he is not titled Markgraf in the document.  "Otto…rex" granted property "in locis Vurmerstat, Otunpach, Gozarstat, Haholtestat
2 CONC …in pago Usiti in comitatu comitis Uuillihelmi" to "vasallo comitisque…Billinc" by charter dated 2 Dec 958[206].  "Otto…rex" granted property "Asundorf marcam et Dornsteti marcam Liubissa…in pago Hassigeuui in comitatu comitis Sig
2 CONC iuuridi…loco Biscopstat…in pago Altgeuui in comitatu comitis Uuillihelmi" to "vassallo Billing" by charter dated 23 Apr 961[207].  "Otto…imperator augustus" granted property "in pago Neletici in comitatu Billingi comitis" to Magde
2 CONC burg St Moritz by charter dated 28 Jul 965[208].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Dux in Saxony 965.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He founded St Michaeliskloster at Lüneburg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of Fulda records the death in 973 of "Heriman dux"[209].  Thietmar records the death of Duke Hermann, father of Bernhard, at Quedlinburg on 1 Apr,  the transportation of his body to Lüneburg, and the refusal by Bruno
2 CONC  Bishop of Verden (maybe his nephew) to allow his burial in church because of his prior excommunication[210].  The necrology of Lüneburg records the death "27 Mar" of "Herimannus dux"[211].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ODA, daughter of --- (-15 Mar <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  The primary source which confirms the name of Hermann's first wife has not so far been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly HILDESUIT, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms the name of Hermann's second wife has not so far been identified.  "Otto…imperator augustus" confirmed the donation of property "aliquando Bilingo nostro co
2 CONC miti…in Neletici…quitquid coniunx sua hereditarii iuris habere" to Magdaburg St Moritz by charter dated 28 Jul 966[212].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Hermann & his [first/second] wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  BERNHARD (-Corvey 9 Feb 1011, bur Lüneburg St Michael).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Bennonis ducis, qui et Bernhardus et Liudigeri comitis et Machtildis comitisse" as brothers and sister of "domna Suanehildis [filia] Herimanni ducis de Liuniburh"[213].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as BERNHARD I Herzog in Sachsen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT b)  LIUTGER (-26 Feb 1011, bur Lüneburg St Michael).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Bennonis ducis, qui et Bernhardus et Liudigeri comitis et Machtildis comitisse" as brothers and sister of "domna Suanehildis [filia] Herimanni ducis de Liuniburh"[214].  "Otto…Romanorum imperat
2 CONC or augustus" gave property "Stipenlo in comitatu ipsius Liutgeri comitis et in pago Westfalon" to "Liutgero comiti" by charter dated 27 Apr 1001 on the petition of "Berenhardi nostri ducis et…capellani nostri"[215].  The Vita Mein
2 CONC werci records the death "IV Kal Apr" of "frater…ducis Bernhardi, comes Liutderus"[216].  The necrology of Lüneburg records the death "26 Feb" of "Liudger com"[217].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m EMMA, daughter of IMMED [III] & his wife Agnes --- (-3 Dec 1038, bur Bremen Cathedral).  The Vita Meinwerci names "Emma" as wife of "comes Liutderus", but does not give her origin[218].  Her parentage is confirmed by Adam of Bre
2 CONC men who names "Emma" as wife of "Liudgerus frater [Benno dux Saxonum]" when recording her husband's death in 1011, calling her "Emma…soror Meginwerki episcopi Padarburnensis" when recording her death and her burial in Bremen Cathe
2 CONC dral[219].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Liutger & his wife had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT c) MECHTILD of Saxony ([942]-Gent 25 May 1008, bur Gent St Peter).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Bennonis ducis, qui et Bernhardus et Liudigeri comitis et Machtildis comitisse" as brothers and sister of "domna Suanehildis [filia] Herimanni ducis de Liuniburh", recording the names of Mechti
2 CONC ld's two husbands[220].  The Genealogica Arnulfi Comitis names "Mathildis, filiam principis Herimanni" as wife of "Balduinum [filius comitis Arnulfi]", specifying that it was hoped that the couple would have many children[221].  T
2 CONC his suggests that their marriage date may have been some years earlier than 961 considering that the Genealogia was supposedly compiled in [951/59], probably during the earlier part of this date range considering which children of
2 CONC  Louis IV King of the West Franks are named in the document[222].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Mathildis comitissa Saxonie" as wife of "Godefridi Ardennensis"[223].  "Heinricus…Romanorum imperator augustus" 
2 CONC confirmed the rights and property of Kloster Mouzon donated by (among others) "dux Fredericus pro anima Ottonis…[et] Godefridus comes et coniux sua Mathildis pro anima sui fratris Adalberonis archiepiscopi" by charter dated 1023[2
2 CONC 24].  The Annales Blandinienses record the death in 1008 of "Mathildis comitissa"[225].  The necrology of Lüneburg records the death "25 May" of "Mattild com"[226].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([951/59]) BAUDOUIN III joint Count of Flanders, son of ARNOUL I "le Grand" Count of Flanders & his second wife Adela de Vermandois [Carolingian] ([940]-1 Jan 962).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ([963]) GODEFROI Comte de Verdun, son of comte GOZELON [Wigeriche] & his wife Uda --- [Matfriede] (-3 Sep 995, bur Gent St Peter). 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)  SCHWANEHILDE [Suanhild] ([945/50]-26 Nov 1014, bur Kloster Jena, transferred 1028 to Naumburg Georgskirche).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annalista Saxo names "domna Suanehildis" as daughter of "Herimanni ducis de Liuniburh", names her brothers "Bennonis ducis et Bernhardus et Liudigeri comitis et Machtildis comitisse" and her two husbands[227].  Her birth date 
2 CONC range is estimated on the basis of her sister being born in [942] and Schwanehilde herself giving birth to seven children by her second husband.  Thietmar records the marriage of Ekkehard and "Swanhild widow of Count Thietmar and 
2 CONC Duke Bernhard's sister"[228].  Thietmar records the death of Suanhild 26 Nov 1014[229].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly THIETMAR [III] Markgraf [der Ostmark], son of CHRISTIAN Graf im Nordthüring- und Schwabengau & his wife Hidda [der Ostmark] (-3 Aug after 979, bur Kloster Nienburg an der Saale).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (before 1000) EKKEHARD [I] Markgraf von Meissen, son of GUNTHER Markgraf im Bischofstum Merseburg & his wife --- (-murdered Pöhlde 30 Apr 1002, bur Kloster Jena, transferred 1028 to Naumburg Georgskirche).
2 CONT
2 CONT e)  IMMA .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not so far been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nun at Herford.  995.
2 CONT
