2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands Project page on Meissen (covering his marriage family):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEISSEN.htm#FriedrichIBrehnadied1191
2 CONT
2 CONT FRIEDRICH [I] von Wettin, son of KONRAD [I] "der Grosse" Graf von Wettin, Brehna, Camburg und Eilenburg, Markgraf der Ober- und Niederlausitz & his wife Luitgard von Elchingen ([27 Feb 1142/19 May 1145]-4 Jan 1191, bur Petersberg)
2 CONC .  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Mi
2 CONC snensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[462].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) brothers "Othonis Misniensis marchionis, Tiderici Orientalis marchionis, Heinrici comitis de Witin, Dedonis comitis
2 CONC  de Rochelez, Friderici comitis de Brene"[463].  
2 CONT *Graf von Brehna 1156. 
2 CONT * Zu Arnoldishagen, Trebus, Loeben, Schweinitz, Jessen, Cloeden, Prettin, Schwedt, Belzig, Zauna, Wiesenburg, Werben and Gommern.  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis records the death in 1181 of "Fridericus comes senior de Brene"[464], but this appears to be an error for 1191. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m HEDWIG of Moravia, daughter of DYPOLD Duke of Moravia & his wife --- von Brandenburg [Ballenstedt] (-Kloster Brehna 19 Feb 1210, bur Kloster Brehna).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Hetwigem filiam Dipoldi cuiusdam nobilis de Boemia, qui fuit patruus Odacari ducis Bohemie" as wife of "Fridericus comes de Brene", and records her death in 1210[465].  The Chronicon Montis Serr
2 CONC eni records that "Hedwigis comitissa vidua Friderici comitis de Brene" founded "monasterium femininum in villa Brene…XVIII Kal Sep [1201]"[466].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni records the death "1210 XI Kal Mar" of "Hethwigis comit
2 CONC issa de Brene" and her burial at Brehna[467].  
2 CONT *She founded Kloster Brehna after 1182. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Friedrich [I] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         OTTO [I] (-23 Dec 1203, bur Kloster Brehna).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Othonem…et Fridericum comitem et filiam Sophiam" as children of "Fridericus comes de Brene" & his wife, specifying that Otto died in youth in 1203[468].  
2 CONT *Graf von Brehna. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         FRIEDRICH [II] (-Acre 16 Oct 1221).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Othonem…et Fridericum comitem et filiam Sophiam" as children of "Fridericus comes de Brene" & his wife[469].  
2 CONT *He succeeded his brother in 1203 as Graf von Brehna.  
2 CONT *Graf von Wettin 1217.  The Chronicon Montis Serreni records the death "Akirs" in 1221 of "Fridericus comes de Brene filius Friderici filii Conradi" specifying that he had become a Knight Templar[470].  
2 CONT *m (1181) JUDITH von Ziegenhain, daughter of FRIEDRICH von Thüringen Graf von Ziegenhain & his wife Liutgard von Ziegenhain (-7 Oct 1220).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Iuditam filiam Friderici comitis de Cigenhagin, fratris
2 CONC  Hermanni comitis Thuringie" as wife of "Fridericus comes iunior", and records her death "1220 Non Oct"[471].  
2 CONT *Graf Friedrich [II] & his wife had four children: Hedwig (Gräfin von Altenburg after 1249), Otto II (b. c1216), Graf von Brehna (1221 - before 1234, minor until 1231), Dietrich I, Graf von Brehna (d. 1234 - 1266/1267), and Lucard
2 CONC is (nun at Brehna in 1220)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         SOPHIE (-after 26 Sep 1235, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Othonem…et Fridericum comitem et filiam Sophiam" as children of "Fridericus comes de Brene" & his wife, specifying that Sophie was "Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam"[477].  The Chronicon Montis S
2 CONC erreni names "Sophia Quiddelingenburgensis abbatissa filia Friderici comitis de Brene filii Conradi marchionis senioris"[478].  
2 CONT *Abbess of Quedlinburg 1203-1224, and 1225. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References:'''
2 CONT
