1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p769.htm#i7690
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich II Herzog von Braunschweig-Kalenberg1 M, #7690, b. circa 1424, d. 5 March 1495
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=14 Apr 2012 Consanguinity Index=0.53%
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich II Herzog von Braunschweig-Kalenberg was born circa 1424. He was the son of Wilhelm I Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg and Cecilie von Hohenzollern.1 He married, firstly, Anne von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen, daughter of Er
2 CONC ich I Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Göttingen, on 1 February 1463. He married, secondly, Margaret von Rietburg, daughter of Conrad V Graf von Rietburg and Jacoba von Neuenah, on 16 November 148
2 CONC 3. He died on 5 March 1495.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich II Herzog von Braunschweig-Kalenberg also went by the nick-name of Friedrich 'the Turbulent'. He was a member of the House of Guelph.1 He gained the title of Herzog von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel in 1482. He gained the ti
2 CONC tle of Herzog von Braunschweig-Kalenberg in 1483.1 He was deposed as Duke of Brunswick-Wolfenbuttel in 1484.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations===
2 CONT [S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 132. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
