1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Stewart, Duke of Ross (30 April 1514, Stirling Castle–18 December 1515, Stirling Castle) was the fourth and last son of King James IV of Scotland and his queen Margaret Tudor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born posthumously, after his father died at the Battle of Flodden Field, during the reign of his infant brother King James V of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in infancy, but during his short life he was heir presumptive to the throne of the Kingdom of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Stewart,_Duke_of_Ross
