2 CONT *[http://e-tidsskrifter.dk/ojs/index.php/historisktidsskrift/article/view/35264/67728 Frederik II's Kalenderoptegnelser for Aarene 1583, 1584 og 1587] In Danish
2 CONT *[http://www.gravsted.dk/person.php?navn=frederik2 Burial] In Danish
2 CONT *[http://danmarkshistorien.dk/leksikon-og-kilder/vis/materiale/frederik-2-1534-1588/ Danmarkshistorien] In Danish
2 CONT *'''King of Denmark and Norway:''' Reign	1559–1588 
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/index/4104411 Christian III] '''Successor:'''  [http://www.geni.com/people/index/4104731 Christian IV]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT FREDERIK of Denmark, son of CHRISTIAN III King of Denmark, King of Norway & his wife Dorothea von Sachsen-Lauenburg (Hadersleben 1 Jul 1534-Antvorskov 4 Apr 1588, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  He succeeded his father in 1559 as FREDER
2 CONC IK II King of Denmark, King of Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Copenhagen 20 Jul 1572) his first cousin, SOPHIE von Mecklenburg-Güstrow, daughter of ULRICH III Herzog von Mecklenburg-Güstrow & his first wife Elisabeth of Denmark (Wismar 4 Sep 1557-Nykøbing 4 Oct 1631, bur Roskilde Cathedra
2 CONC l). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederik III & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ELISABETH Pss of Denmark (Kolding 25 Aug 1573-Braunschweig 19 Jul 1626, bur Wolfenbüttel Beatæ Mariæ Virginæ).  m (Copenhagen, Kronborg Castle 19 Apr 1590) as his second wife, HEINRICH JULIUS Herzog von Braunschweig-Wol
2 CONC fenbüttel, son of JULIUS Herzog von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel & his wife Hedwig von Brandenburg (Hessen 15 Oct 1564-Prague 20 Jul 1613, bur Wolfenbüttel Beatae Mariae Virginae). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ANNA Pss of Denmark (Scanderborg Castle, Jutland 14 Oct 1574-Hampton Court Palace 4 Mar 1619, bur Westminster Abbey).  Crowned Queen of Scotland 17 May 1590 at Holyrood Abbey, Edinburgh.  Crowned Queen of England 25 Jul
2 CONC  1603 at Westminster Abbey.  m (by proxy Kronborg Castle Copenhagen 20/24 Aug 1589, in person Oslo 23 Nov 1589, and in person again Kronborg Castle 21 Jan 1590) JAMES VI King of Scotland, son of HENRY Stuart Lord Darnley Duke of A
2 CONC lbany & his wife Mary Queen of Scotland (Edinburgh Castle 19 Jun 1566-Theobalds Park, Herts 27 Mar 1625, bur Westminster Abbey).  He succeeded in 1603 as JAMES I King of England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         CHRISTIAN Prince of Denmark (Frederiksborg 12 Apr 1577-Rosenborg 28 Feb/9 Mar 1648, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  He succeeded his father in 1588 as CHRISTIAN IV King of Denmark, King of Norway.  m firstly (Hadersleben 7 De
2 CONC c 1597) ANNA KATHARINA von Brandenburg, daughter of JOACHIM FRIEDRICH Markgraf von Brandenburg [later JOACHIM FRIEDRICH Elector of Brandenburg] & his first wife Katharina von Brandenburg-Küstrin (Halle an der Saale 26 Jun 1575-Cop
2 CONC enhagen 8 Apr 1612, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  m secondly (31 Dec 1615, divorced 1630) KIRSTEN Munk, daughter of LUDWIK Munk & his wife Ellen Marsvin (6 Jul 1598-Boller 19 Apr 1658).  She was created Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein 1
2 CONC 629.  Christian IV & his first wife had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         FREDERIK Prince of Denmark (Frederiksborg Castle 15 Aug 1599-Roskilde 9 Sep 1599, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         CHRISTIAN Prince of Denmark (Copenhagen Castle 10 Apr 1603-Schloß Görbitz bei Dresden 2 Jun 1647).  Crown Prince of Denmark.  m (Copenhagen Castle 5 Oct 1634) as her first husband, MAGDALENE SIBYLLE Herzogin von Sachsen
2 CONC , daughter of JOHANN GEORG I Elector of Saxony & his second wife Magdalene Sibylle Pss von Preußen (Dresden 23 Dec 1617-Altenburg 6 Jan 1668, bur Altenburg Schloßkirche).  She married secondly (Dresden 11 Oct 1652) as his second w
2 CONC ife, Friedrich Wilhelm II Herzog von Sachsen-Altenburg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         SOPHIA Pss of Denmark (Kronborg Castle 4 Jan 1605-Copenhagen 7 Sep 1605, bur Roskilde Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         ELISABETH Pss of Denmark (Copenhagen Castle 13 Mar 1606-Skanderborg 24 Oct 1608, bur Roskilde Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         FREDERIK Prince of Denmark (Schloß Hadersleben 18 Mar 1609-Copenhagen Castle 9 Feb 1670, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  Crown Prince of Denmark from 1647, on the death of his older brother.  He succeeded his father in 1648 a
2 CONC s FREDERIK III King of Denmark, King of Norway.   
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT f)          ULRIK Prince of Denmark (Copenhagen Castle 2 Feb 1611-killed in battle Lager near Schweidnitz 22 Aug 1633, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian IV & his second wife had ten children:
2 CONT
2 CONT g)         ANNA KATHARINA Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Frederiksborg 10 Aug 1618-Frederiksborg 20 Aug 1633). 
2 CONT
2 CONT h)         SOPHIA ELISABETH Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Skanderborg 20 Sep 1619-Boller 29 Apr 1657, bur Odense St Knuds Kirke).  m (Copenhagen 10 Oct 1634) CHRISTIAN von Pentz zu Neudorf, son of --- (-1651).  Graf von Pentz 163
2 CONC 6.  
2 CONT
2 CONT i)           ELEONORA CHRISTINA Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Frederiksborg 8 Jul 1621-Maribo Kloster, Laaland Island 16 Mar 1698).  m (Copenhagen 9 Oct 1636) CORFIZ Ulfeldt, from Saltø, son of --- (-near Basel 20 Feb 1664, bur N
2 CONC eunberg am Rhein Kloster).  Greve Ulfeldt 1641.  Danish ambassador.  He served in the Swedish army 1657.  He drowned in the River Rhine and was buried under a false name[881].  
2 CONT
2 CONT j)           WOLDEMAR CHRISTIAN Graf von Schleswig-Holstein (Frederiksborg 26 Jul 1622-killed in battle Lublin 20 Feb 1656). 
2 CONT
2 CONT k)          ELISABETH AUGUSTA Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Kromborg Castle 28 Dec 1623-9 Aug 1677).  m (Copenhagen 27 Oct 1639) HANS Lindenow, son of --- (-Copenhagen 29 May 1659).  Danish State Counsellor.  
2 CONT
2 CONT l)           FREDERIK CHRISTIAN Graf von Schleswig-Holstein (Frederiksborg 26 Apr 1625-Dalum Kloster, Fünen 17 Jul 1627). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m)        CHRISTIANE Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Haderslevhuus 15 Jul 1626-1670 before 6 May).  Twin with her sister Hedwig.  m (Copenhagen 6 Nov 1642) HANNIBAL Sehested, son of --- (-Passy near Paris 13 Sep 1666).  Governor of
2 CONC  Norway.  Danish ambassador at the French court.  He was created Comte de Sehested in France in 1663.  
2 CONT
2 CONT n)         HEDWIG Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Haderslevhuus 15 Jul 1626-Christianstadt 5 Oct 1678).  Twin with her sister Christiane.  m (Copenhagen 6 Nov 1642) EBBE Ulfeld, son of --- (-Skivehus Mar 1654). 
2 CONT
2 CONT o)         MARIE CATHARINA Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Copenhagen 29 May 1628-Copenhagen 1 Sep 1628). 
2 CONT
2 CONT p)         DOROTHEA ELISABETH Gräfin von Schleswig-Holstein (Kronborg Castle 1 Sep 1629-Köln 18 Mar 1687).  Carmelite nun at Köln 1655. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         ULRIK Prince of Denmark (Kolding 30 Dec 1578-Rühm 27 Mar 1624, bur Bützow Stadtkirche, transferred 1642 to Roskilde Cathedral).  Canon at Strasbourg Cathedral 1593.  m as her first husband, KATHARINA Hahn, daughter of O
2 CONC TTO Hahn & his wife Brigitte von Trotha.  She married secondly Nikolaus Hermann von Nidrum.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         JOHAN Prince of Denmark (Hadersleben 26 Jul 1583-Moscow 28 Oct 1602, bur Moscow German Church, transferred 1637 to Roskilde Cathedral).  m (1602) XENIA Borisovna Godunova, daughter of BORIS Godunov Tsar of all Russias &
2 CONC  his wife Maria Grigorievna Skuratova-Belskaia (1582-1622).  This marriage was arranged by the bride's father in an attempt to boost his international prestige when facing mounting domestic problems in Russia, but the bridegroom d
2 CONC ied soon after the marriage[882]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         AUGUSTA Pss of Denmark (Kolding 8 Apr 1580-Husum 5 Feb 1639, bur Schleswig Cathedral).  m (Copenhagen 30 Aug 1596) JOHANN ADOLF Herzog von Schleswig-Holstein in Gottorp, son of ADOLF Herzog von Schleswig-Holstein in Got
2 CONC torp & his wife Christina von Hessen (Gottorf 27 Feb 1575-Gottorf 31 Mar 1616, bur Gottorf). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         HEDWIG Pss of Denmark (Frederiksborg Castle 5 Aug 1581-Lichtenberg 26 Nov 1641, bur Freiberg Cathedral).  m (Dresden 12 Sep 1602) CHRISTIAN II Elector of Saxony, son of CHRISTIAN I Elector of Saxony & his wife Sophie vo
2 CONC n Brandenburg (Dresden 23 Sep 1583-Dresden 23 Jun 1611, bur Freiberg). 
2 CONT
2 CONT  https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DENMARK.htm
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
