1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Count John VII of Oldenburg and Delmenhorst (nicknamed "the Dike Builder"; 9 September 1540 in Oldenburg – 12 November 1603 in Oldenburg) was a member of the House of Oldenburg and was the ruling Count of County of
2 CONC  Oldenburg from 1573 until his death. His parents were Count Anthony I of Oldenburg and Sophie of Saxe-Lauenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT LIFE
2 CONT In 1573, John VII inherited the County of Oldenburg from his father. In 1575, he inherited the Lordship of Jever from Maria of Jever, despite objections by Count Edzard II of East Frisia. In 1577, he had to concede the revenue fro
2 CONC m Harpstedt, Delmenhorst, Varel and some minor castles to his younger brother Anthony II for a 10-year period. In 1597, the Aulic Council ordered that the County of Delmenhorst be split off from Oldenburg; this separation would la
2 CONC st until 1647.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1596, John VII attempted to dam the Schwarze Brack, in order to create a land link from Oldenburg to Jever. He had to cancel this project under pressure of Edzard II. John VII nevertheless earned the nickname "dike builder" wit
2 CONC h his costly land reclamation projects in Butjadingen and the Jade Bight.
2 CONT
2 CONT He reorganized the administration and the judiciary and modernized the organization of the Lutheran Church in Oldenburg. His superintendent Hamelmann unified the Lutheran confession.
2 CONT
2 CONT John VII died in 1603 and was succeeded by his son Anthony Günther.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT In 1576 John VII married Countess Elisabeth of Schwarzburg (1541–1612), daughter of Günther XL, Count of Schwarzburg. John and Elisabeth had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1578–1580)
2 CONT Anne (1579–1639)
2 CONT Elizabeth (1581–1619)
2 CONT Catherine (1582–1644), married in 1633 Augustus of Saxe-Lauenburg
2 CONT Anthony Günther (1583–1667), succeeding Count of Oldenburg
2 CONT Magdalene (1585–1657), heiress of Jever; married in 1612 Rudolph, Prince of Anhalt-Zerbst.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich Wilhelm Schaer (1974). "Johann XVI. (Vii.)". Neue Deutsche Biographie (in German). Vol. 10. Berlin: Duncker & Humblot. pp. 508–509. (full text online).
2 CONT Hans Friedl, Wolfgang Günther, Hilke Günther-Arndt and Heinrich Schmidt (eds.): Biographisches Handbuch zur Geschichte des Landes Oldenburg, Oldenburg, 1992, ISBN 3-89442-135-5
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_VII,_Count_of_Oldenburg
