0 @N6000000003949860631@ NOTE The first Burgrave who is mentioned in the records, in the year 1122, is Otto von Rheineck. He bore the name of the Castle as was customary at that period. The search for the family names of holders of fiefs in these times is diff
1 CONC cult, and maybe entirely vain. As therefore after the building of the Castle by Archbishop Remold, the new Burggrafen are merely called "Rheineck",—the name which the dignity of the castellany conferred upon them;—the question whe
1 CONC ther the Archbishop reinstated the family which had incurred the anger of the Emperor Conrad, must remain unanswered.  "The Rhine"
1 CONT  By W. O. von Horn
