0 @N6000000002187780937@ NOTE Dorothea of Brandenburg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Dorothea of Brandenburg (1430/1431 – November 10, 1495) was the consort of Christopher of Bavaria and Christian I of Denmark. She is also known as Dorothea of Hohenzollern and as Dorothy Achillies. She was queen of Denmark (1445-1
1 CONC 448 and 1449-1481), Norway (1445-1448 and 1450-1481) and Sweden (1447-1448 and 1457-1464) two times each.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Biography
1 CONT Dorothea was born in 1430 or 1431 to John, Margrave of Brandenburg-Kulmbach and Barbara, Duchess of Anhalt (1405-1465). She had two sisters: Barbara (1423-1481, who became the Marchioness of Mantua, and Elisabeth (14??-1451), who 
1 CONC married Joachim I Mlodszy, Duke of Pomerania (14??-1451).
1 CONT
1 CONT She married, on 12 September 1445, Christopher of Bavaria, the King of Denmark from 1440-1448, Sweden from 1441-1448 and Norway from 1442-1448. The wedding was held in Copenhagen. She was crowned queen of the three kingdoms on 14 
1 CONC September 1445.
1 CONT
1 CONT After Christopher's death, Dorothea married the next elected king, King Christian I of Denmark, on 28 October 1449. In 1457, she became queen of Sweden for the second time and was crowned in Uppsala Cathedral.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dorothea was given very large estates in Sweden at her first wedding, which she lost control over in 1464. For the rest of her life, she fought to regain control over them, and also asked for the help of the Pope. She was given Ho
1 CONC lstein as her fief, and in 1481, she made her youngest son Frederik regent there. In 1488 she visited the Pope in Rome. She is described as economical and energetic and she is believed to have exerted political influence.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT Oluf (1450-1451) 
1 CONT Canute (1451-1455) 
1 CONT John (Hans) (1455-1513), Duke of Schleswig-Holstein, King of Denmark, Norway and Sweden 
1 CONT Margarete (1456-1486), married King James III of Scotland in 1469 
1 CONT King Frederik I of Denmark, Norway and Sweden (1471-1533) 
1 CONT Dorothea died on 25 November 1495, and is interred next to her second husband in Roskilde Cathedral.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Herman Lindqvist, "Historien om Sverige" (In Swedish) 
1 CONT Åke Ohlmarks "Alla Sveriges drottningar" (In Swedish) 
