0 @N6000000002187746650@ NOTE Dirk VI, Count of Holland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk VI, Count of Holland between 1121 and 1157. Born c. 1114, died 5 August 1157. He was the son of Floris II. His son Floris III succeeded him. He married Sofie, Countess of Rheineck, Salm and Bentheim.
1 CONT
1 CONT When his father died he was only 7 years old, and his mother, Petronilla of Saxony governed as a regent. While he was young there was a rebellion from the West Frisians from the districts of Oostergoo and Westergoo, helped by Flor
1 CONC is, his younger brother. They were defeated in 1131, and in October 1132 Floris was killed.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had supported his relative Lothair of Saxony against Henry V and parts of Holland were recovered that had been occupied by Utrecht. With help from Conrad II he was able to get a candidate of his own recognised as being the bish
1 CONC op of Utrecht.
1 CONT
1 CONT He went on a crusade to the Holy Land in 1139.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT External links
1 CONT Biography at worldroots 
1 CONT Biography at allbiographies 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Floris II Count of Holland
1 CONT 1121 - 1157 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Floris III 
0 @N6000000003949860418@ NOTE Before he took over as ruler, his mother Petronilla was regent. In 1123 she was involved in the uprising against Emperor Heinrich V of Germany, but was defeated in a battle. Things improved when Lotharius III became Emperor, her h
1 CONC alf-brother. In 1130, Dirk could add Rijnland to his area which included the city of Leiden, the former property of the Bishops of Utrecht. He had to fight his brother, Floris "the Black", see below.
