0 @N6000000002187746574@ NOTE Floris III, Count of Holland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Floris III of Holland ( 1141 - August 1, 1190),Count of Holland from 1157 to 1190. He was a son of Dirk VI and Sophie of Luxemburg, heiress of Bentheim.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Life
1 CONT On September 28, 1162 he married Ada, sister of king William I of Scotland, also known as William the Lion. The county of Holland adopted from him the rampant lion in the coat of arms and the name of William.
1 CONT
1 CONT Floris III was a loyal vassal to Frederick I Barbarossa. He accompanied the emperor on two expeditions to Italy in 1158 and 1176-1178.
1 CONT
1 CONT The emperor gave Floris the toll right of Geervliet, the most important toll station in Holland at that time. This was actually the legalisation of an existing situation, because the counts of Holland had charged tolls illegally s
1 CONC ince the start of the 11th century.
1 CONT
1 CONT During his reign Floris III had troubles with West-Friesland and a war with Philip count of Flanders concerning their respective rights in West Zeeland, in which he was beaten. In 1170 a great flood caused immense devastation in t
1 CONC he north and helped to form the Zuider Zee.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1189 Floris accompanied Frederick Barbarossa upon the third Crusade, of which he was a distinguished leader. He died in 1190 at Antioch of pestilence and was buried there.
1 CONT
1 CONT Two sons of Floris III became count of Holland: Dirk VII in 1190 and William I in 1203.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married 28 August 1162 with Ada of Scotland, daughter of Henry of Scotland, 3rd Earl of Huntingdon and Ada de Warenne. They children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk VII, Count of Holland. 
1 CONT William I, Count of Holland. 
1 CONT Floris (d. 1210), a canon at Utrecht and Middelburg. 
1 CONT Baldwin (d. 1204). 
1 CONT Ada (d. after 1205), married 1176 Margrave Otto I of Brandenburg. 
1 CONT Margaret (d. after 1203), married 1182 Count Dietrich IV of Cleves. 
1 CONT Elizabeth 
1 CONT Hedwig 
1 CONT Agnes (d. 1228), Abbess at Rijnsburg. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Dirk VI Count of Holland
1 CONT 1157 - 1190 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Dirk VII 
0 @N6000000003403184259@ NOTE [huntingdonhenry_descendents10_fromrootsweb_bartont.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Count of Holland, Earl of Ross. (Weis 100-25-h).
0 @N6000000003949860408@ NOTE Florence III, Count of Holland, 1st son and heir of Count Thierri VI by his wife Sophie, daughter of Otto, Count of Reineck, in 1162 m. Ada, sister of Malcolm IV. The Earldom of Ross, possibly then created for that purpose, is sai
1 CONC d to have been given him as her marriage portion. The Count took the Cross with the Emperor Frederick in 1188; the Emperor was buried in Antioch in 1190, and the Count soon afterwards. His widow was living in 1206. [Complete Peera
1 CONC ge XI:140-1]
1 CONT The county of Holland adopted from him the rampant lion in the coat of arms and the name of William.
1 CONT Floris III was a loyal vassal to Frederick I Barbarossa. He accompanied the emperor on two expeditions to Italy in 1158 and 1176-1178. Frederick thanked him by making Floris part of the imperial nobility.
1 CONT The emperor gave Floris the toll right of Geervliet, the most important toll station in Holland at that time. This was actually the legalisation of an existing situation, because the counts of Holland had charged tolls illegally s
1 CONC ince the start of the 11th century.
1 CONT Many farmers came to Holland to turn the swamps into agricultural lands. Dikes and dams were build and the border between Holland and the bishopric of Utrecht had to be determined. There was a dispute between Floris and the bishop
1 CONC  of Utrecht about a new dam in the Rhine at Zwammerdam in 1165, which had to be settled by emperor Frederick. The brother of Floris, Baldwin became bishop of Utrecht in 1178.
1 CONT War broke out between Flanders and Holland. Count Philip of Flanders wanted to have Zeeland. Floris was captured in Brugge and had to accept Flemish overlordship in Zeeland as ransom in 1167.
1 CONT During his reign Floris III had troubles with West Friesland and a war with Philip count of Flanders concerning their respective rights in West Zeeland, in which he was beaten. In 1170 a great flood caused immense devastation in t
1 CONC he north and helped to form the Zuider Zee.
1 CONT In 1189 Floris accompanied Frederick Barbarossa upon the third Crusade, of which he was a distinguished leader. In May 1190 Floris commanded the army that stormed Iconium (now Konya, Turkey)  He died in 1190 at Antioch of pestilen
1 CONC ce and was buried there.
